SOAPBOX: Started the contest at 21:00 due to other obligations earlier in the day. Once I figured out using the NA VHF mode option, life was easier. I also had to make a few minor adjustments like adding the FT4 frequencies to the WSJT software. Used N1MM+ and internal WSJT-X program. Worked well. If my start sequence was started too late WSJT would freeze up and lock the radio in TX. Had to exit the program and restart to get the radio the unlock in the TX mode. After about a dozen times of "lock-up" my rhythm improved and clock awareness improved. Learning curve schooling. Overall a fun time. Mindless computer contesting at its best. Switched between FT4 and FT8 to catch a few extra multis that paid off but FT4 rocks.
